input.prompt:
You are the lead-pm role. Record the decision into the architecture decision record's Document History.

Write into the record's Document History one review entry per round with its verdict and, from judge_log, the screening judge's model and prompt version, then a state entry carrying the decision and its reasons. Set the record's status: "checked" on pass, "returned" on fail with the criterion named, "pending-definition" on definition-change. On "definition-change", write a review entry stating the gap into the Document History of the definition the decision names; return that file's path as definition and the entry's text as gap_entry. Otherwise return both empty. Return the artifact.

Return each declared output on its own line as `<name>: <value>` — artifact, gap_entry, definition — a list as a JSON array, a value with line breaks as a JSON string; these lines close your reply.

---

INPUTS:
decision: {
  "verdict": "pass",
  "reasons": "the one decision (a run's cost row in a new lead-shop artifact beside the session record, written by a runtime step after collect, the harness's report the only source, blank never estimated) holds each criterion; the three wobbly findings are repaired in the revise; the record stays at 2,544 words, long but within the criteria."
}

artifact: decisions/adr-2026-09-08-run-cost-artifact.md

round_log: [
  {
    "verdict": "findings",
    "findings": [
      {
        "criterion": "principles",
        "quoted_text": "The session_record data value is typed $ref: session-record, from: pkg:shopsystem-knowledge/session-record — a package this shop does not own. ... single-source-of-truth: the session-record schema is owned by pkg:shopsystem-knowledge, fetched through that package's own contract tool, not by this shop; a fact this shop does not own gets no second home written into it. ... contracts-between-contexts — no Bounded Context is touched; nothing here reaches across a contract.",
        "change": "Name what pkg:shopsystem-knowledge is in the Bounded Context/shop taxonomy, or narrow the claim from 'no Bounded Context is touched' to 'this decision adds no new touch beyond the existing reference'.",
        "confidence": "wobbly"
      },
      {
        "criterion": "scenario 1 (one decision)",
        "quoted_text": "by a new runtime step (never an agent step) added at session-handoff-process's collect step, the step that already produces the session record the artifact sits beside ... a new runtime step is added at (or immediately beside) collect, reading the run's anchor and the harness's usage report and writing the row.",
        "change": "State one placement for the new step (inside collect vs. a distinct adjacent step) consistently in the Decision and the Consequences sections.",
        "confidence": "wobbly"
      },
      {
        "criterion": "scenario 2 (evidence)",
        "quoted_text": "the delivered router already reads the harness's own usage report per resumed segment and per launched role (v9's delivery history, v7).",
        "change": "Name the specific artifact and version/entry this citation points to instead of a bare 'v9 ... v7' parenthetical.",
        "confidence": "wobbly"
      }
    ]
  }
]

judge_log: ["claude-sonnet-5, cold-reviewer role (compiled from basis/roles/cold-reviewer.md), task instructions dated 2026-09-08"]

